Feature List:
- Add a TheoryBox to the Add Blocks button in the Editor.
- Add "SectionedBox" Blocks to the Editor. It has two behaviours: In Combos/Techs Group section, and In everywhere else. In Combos/Techs Group section, right now you can only create new TheoryBox Blocks when you are making new things in a Combos Group, Now it gives you the choice to select between TheoryBox and SectionedBox. When SectionedBox is used in a Combos/Techs Group, it will wrap itself in the same box wrapper that TheoryBox use. It will have an Introduction, Sections, and Contents in Sections. Introduction and Contents in Sections both use the Accordion recursive logic to hold other Blocks inside it. Sections is just add/remove tab. Appearance-wise, it is a box with some words above, then below it is a bunch of switchable tabs, and the content of the currently loaded tab (default to first tab). When used anywhere else, remove the box wrapper, so SectionedBox blends in nicely with other Block elements (Also to stop wrapper on wrapper styling).
